ligned}Φ(-0.63) & =P(Z\\le -0.63) \\\\  & =P(Z\\ge 0.63) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<0.63) \\\\  & =1-P(Z\\le 0.63) \\\\  & =1-Φ(0.63) \\\\  & =1-0.7357 \\\\  & =0.2643\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.63<Z<0.63) & =Φ(0.63)-Φ(-0.63) \\\\  & =0.7357-0.2643 \\\\  & =0.4714.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535768 true] [17592186365360 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365361 13194139535768 true] [17592186365360 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365362 13194139535768 true] [17592186365360 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535768 true] [17592186365360 1041 "field-1" 13194139535768 true] [17592186365360 1104 #edb/ref 17592186365362 13194139535768 true] [17592186365360 1110 #uuid "714a5d94-1904-53e6-9913-a93da697a8da" 13194139535768 true] [17592186365361 1034 "0.7357" 13194139535768 true] [17592186365361 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535768 true] [17592186365361 1111 #uuid "8ee43f02-a302-595a-b20e-7372e1a8c914" 13194139535768 true] [17592186365362 1034 "0.4714" 13194139535768 true] [17592186365362 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535768 true] [17592186365362 1111 #uuid "736bb855-85f4-5f7b-bc75-ee71606f7691" 13194139535768 true] [17592186365363 1017 #edb/ref 17592186365364 13194139535768 true] [17592186365363 1089 "q-330903" 13194139535768 true] [17592186365363 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535768 true] [17592186365363 1100 "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(-1.55<Z<1.55).$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.4\\,$ | $\\,0.9236\\,$ | $\\,0.9251\\,$ | $\\,0.9265\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.5\\,$ | $\\,0.9370\\,$ | $\\,0.9382\\,$ | $\\,0.9394\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.6\\,$ | $\\,0.9484\\,$ | $\\,0.9495\\,$ | $\\,0.9505\\,$ |\n\n$P(-1.55<Z<1.55)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535768 true] [17592186365363 1113 #uuid "c14c23d5-7455-50af-9191-550faf7f7f76" 131